    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0718" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg598"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Chargé to Acting Secretary of State
                        Adee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Japan</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July 31,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Adee</hi>: Referring to your note of the
                    29th instant, relative to the request for permission to return to Russia for two
                    lieutenants and three sublieutenants aboard the Russian vessels now interned at
                    Manila, on account of illness, I have the honor to inform you that the Japanese
                    Government would not have objection to the desired permission being given to the
                    said officers under such conditions as have been exacted by the United States
                    Government in former similar cases.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eki Hioki</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
